{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And a pure man shall gather.</b> According to the plain sense, this is the order of the verse: since the one who burns it has already become impure, he himself shall gather the cow's ashes — so why would we bring another priest to gather, who would also become impure? Therefore it says <b>and a pure man shall gather</b> — that one must seek out a pure man to gather." "<b>And place it outside the camp.</b> Rashi explained: this refers to that which is on the Mount of Anointing. The high priests purify from it for other cows — meaning, for those who become impure through the burning of other cows."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {1 "The phrase 'high priests purify from it for other cows' is understood to mean that the ashes gathered by high priests at the Mount of Anointing are used for purifying those who become impure through the burning of subsequent red heifers."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:42.416859293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}